{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool","id":1301503,"title":"Storyteller Willpower Pool","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-31T21:22:14-07:00","id":1301503,"title":"Storyteller Willpower Pool","content":"I've read the great suggestion of the Storyteller having a single Willpower pool that all NPC expenditures must come from. The reason is fairly obvious - RAW there is no drawback from any given npc spending willpower like crazy since they don't exist when off stage, while pcs are impacted in future scenes for their expenditures. Having a single pool lets the Storyteller balance npc willpower expenditures as a resource just like players do.<br /> <br /> Has anyone run with this rule hack before. What size pool do you recommend? Any special rules on replenishment you recommend? I'm thinking right now a pool of 10-15, with a point replenished every time a new significant npc is introduced, and 1 point replenished an in-game day. I may also apply the house rule that for every 3 successes on a pc's influence roll of an npc above difficulty/resolve, an additional wp from the ST's pool is required to ignore the influence. This rule would not apply to player characters resisting influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:03:26-07:00","id":1301510,"title":"","content":"I like the idea better then the Core's method of just saying 'try not to be a dick and have your NPCs spam willpower like crazy every time you theoretically have an opportunity to as written'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:06:01-07:00","id":1301511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool#post1301503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read the great suggestion of the Storyteller having a single Willpower pool that all NPC expenditures must come from. The reason is fairly obvious - RAW there is no drawback from any given npc spending willpower like crazy since they don't exist when off stage, while pcs are impacted in future scenes for their expenditures. Having a single pool lets the Storyteller balance npc willpower expenditures as a resource just like players do.<br /> <br /> Has anyone run with this rule hack before. What size pool do you recommend? Any special rules on replenishment you recommend? I'm thinking right now a pool of 10-15, with a point replenished every time a new significant npc is introduced, and 1 point replenished an in-game day. I may also apply the house rule that for every 3 successes on a pc's influence roll of an npc above difficulty/resolve, an additional wp from the ST's pool is required to ignore the influence. This rule would not apply to player characters resisting influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this make sense? This just sounds like a stupid easily abusable rule where players just work on wasting irrelevant NPC's willpower to get someone who matters. Why do that when it should be logical who negates willpower or not. NPC's should be spending willpower as necessary but trying to convince a farmer to help you should be much easier than a dragon blooded who knows you are anathema. You should use have NPC's use willpower as it would matter to the character or at the very least relevance of the NPC rather than just having them fire off willpower for every little thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:13:38-07:00","id":1301513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301511#post1301511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this make sense? This just sounds like a stupid easily abusable rule where players just work on wasting irrelevant NPC's willpower to get someone who matters. Why do that when it should be logical who negates willpower or not. NPC's should be spending willpower as necessary but trying to convince a farmer to help you should be much easier than a dragon blooded who knows you are anathema. You should use have NPC's use willpower as it would matter to the character or at the very least relevance of the NPC rather than just having them fire off willpower for every little thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense because it recognizes willpower as a meta currency rather than pretending it actually reflects something inherent to the characters that is drained. And the current rules hinge on treating willpower as a resource pool that the expenditures from need to be balanced, but it just isn\u2019t for npcs because it\u2019s effectively unlimited for all of them by any reasonable measure relative to pcs, so whether a social influence on an npc EVER works is purely up to storyteller fiat rather than the player character\u2019s actual rolls or powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:17:46-07:00","id":1301515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301511#post1301511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this make sense? This just sounds like a stupid easily abusable rule where players just work on wasting irrelevant NPC's willpower to get someone who matters. Why do that when it should be logical who negates willpower or not. NPC's should be spending willpower as necessary but trying to convince a farmer to help you should be much easier than a dragon blooded who knows you are anathema. You should use have NPC's use willpower as it would matter to the character or at the very least relevance of the NPC rather than just having them fire off willpower for every little thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are they going to do that, exactly? Become known as the weirdos that go to towns and try to persuade random towns people to dance naked in traffic before talking to the mayor about joining their rebellion against the Realm?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:24:42-07:00","id":1301517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301515#post1301515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are they going to do that, exactly? Become known as the weirdos that go to towns and try to persuade random towns people to dance naked in traffic before talking to the mayor about joining their rebellion against the Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was about to add: why would the Storyteller spend willpower from the pool for the irrelevant npc? If the PCs want to go around using superhuman social abilities to bully people for no reason in setting, there are plenty of in setting consequences for that.<br /> <br /> As for the farmer vs the Dragon Blooded - this system actually encourages treating them differently since the storyteller is incentivized to conserve willpower for the Dragon Blooded and NOT have the farmer resist. RAW, there is no measure to encourage treating either\u2019s willpower as a finite resource the way pc willpower is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:28:16-07:00","id":1301518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301517#post1301517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was about to add: why would the Storyteller spend willpower from the pool for the irrelevant npc? If the PCs want to go around using superhuman social abilities to bully people for no reason in setting, there are plenty of in setting consequences for that.<br /> <br /> As for the farmer vs the Dragon Blooded - this system actually encourages treating them differently since the storyteller is incentivized to conserve willpower for the Dragon Blooded and NOT have the farmer resist. RAW, there is no measure to encourage treating either\u2019s willpower as a finite resource the way pc willpower is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know why you'd block them if it's trival anyway also if you exploit their intimacies there is little to no way for them to resist anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:52:42-07:00","id":1301524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301517#post1301517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was about to add: why would the Storyteller spend willpower from the pool for the irrelevant npc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because if it makes sense of the minor NPC to resist, they need to spend WP to resist.<br /> <br /> To me the biggest issue with this idea, is that the pool size is impossible to set at a good level without radically changing the way points work in the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> The pool is either too small, and the ST doesn't have the WP to spend on resisting all the times it makes sense for a NPC to try, or it's too big and you effectively have the same situation as the RAW.<br /> <br /> I think to get this to work you'd need something far more thorough in the 'doom pool' variety of meta-currencies where there's a give and take as players fill the doom pool to do stuff calibrated to give the ST the points they need, and then the ST doesn't need such an arbitrarily large pool that it might as well be infinite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:59:45-07:00","id":1301526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301524#post1301524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because if it makes sense of the minor NPC to resist, they need to spend WP to resist.<br /> <br /> To me the biggest issue with this idea, is that the pool size is impossible to set at a good level without radically changing the way points work in the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> The pool is either too small, and the ST doesn't have the WP to spend on resisting all the times it makes sense for a NPC to try, or it's too big and you effectively have the same situation as the RAW.<br /> <br /> I think to get this to work you'd need something far more thorough in the 'doom pool' variety of meta-currencies where there's a give and take as players fill the doom pool to do stuff calibrated to give the ST the points they need, and then the ST doesn't need such an arbitrarily large pool that it might as well be infinite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that\u2019s the problem i\u2019m having - willpower is supposed to reflect an individualized pool of strength, but that pool is balanced on the assumption it\u2019s a finite resource where spending it has consequences going forward, and for npcs (I.e. virtually all cases of resisting pc\u2019s influence) that just isn\u2019t the case.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d argue that a case where \u201cbut it makes sense for this character to resist, but they can\u2019t because the storyteller is saving willpower\u201d would reflect the \u201cthey themselves don\u2019t have the willpower to resist at this moment.\u201d PCs go into encounters will compromised willpower pools all the time, why wouldn\u2019t npcs from an in-setting perspective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:13:21-07:00","id":1301528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301524#post1301524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because if it makes sense of the minor NPC to resist, they need to spend WP to resist.<br /> <br /> To me the biggest issue with this idea, is that the pool size is impossible to set at a good level without radically changing the way points work in the game as a whole.<br /> <br /> The pool is either too small, and the ST doesn't have the WP to spend on resisting all the times it makes sense for a NPC to try, or it's too big and you effectively have the same situation as the RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think it's even worse than that, because if you have one big pool then the PCs can't easily drain some fidgety cowardly bureaucrat of his willpower because he's got the whole Storyteller pool to play with, which he shouldn't have, he should have like 2, maybe even 1.<br /> <br /> Also, there actually are some cases where spending willpower like it's going out of style is pretty warranted for NPCs. Like if you're a grizzled mercenary captain, and you agree to a duel to the death with some upstart punk who thinks he's going to take control of your mercenary force, for instance. Betting your life and leadership on the outcome of this duel...buuut then a glittering castemark of the Dawn appears on his forehead and you realize that he's actually a Forsaken anathema. There's few actions you're going to take after that point that won't have a willpower spent on them.<br /> <br /> Or alternatively if you're a spy for the Mask of Winters showing up to a fancy gala, and somebody pointedly asks you if you've ever been to Thorns, and then stare at you with burning intensity, looking for the faintest hint of panic that you may have been caught out. Totally appropriate there.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you really wanted to do it though, I'd say make it at least fair and give the ST pool 5 for every player there, because they have at least that, and also get back one for each player every in game day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:55:42-07:00","id":1301535,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the big problem with this is that a ST who is wanting to be able to abuse the system by having NPCs spam willpower for things they really shouldn't by the core rules suggestion is unlikely to agree to being shackled by house rules limiting their ability to do that. I can see why people might be worried about creating the opposite situation where the players try to metagame and willpower tap the ST instead but its a lot easier for a ST to shut that down (or let them but then make them suffer for running around randomly fucking with nobodies for no in character reason except being massive dicks) then it is for a player to do anything about a ST abusing the WP rules as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:00:46-07:00","id":1301537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301535#post1301535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the big problem with this is that a ST who is wanting to be able to abuse the system by having NPCs spam willpower for things they really shouldn't by the core rules suggestion is unlikely to agree to being shackled by house rules limiting their ability to do that. I can see why people might be worried about creating the opposite situation where the players try to metagame and willpower tap the ST instead but its a lot easier for a ST to shut that down (or let them but then make them suffer for running around randomly fucking with nobodies for no in character reason except being massive dicks) then it is for a player to do anything about a ST abusing the WP rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ST abusing the WP rules would do it any way he could. I don't know why you act as if changing this would actually alter an ST who doesn't know how to run the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:06:23-07:00","id":1301539,"title":"","content":"Thanks for agreeing that terrible STs are terrible STs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:29:20-07:00","id":1301542,"title":"","content":"I think a bit more than just agree that terrible STs are terrible, is that a lot of us appreciate that RPG game design is moving away from the idea of trying to use the mechanics to curtail terrible players/STs.<br /> <br /> While I'd agree that the NPC rules could be better (and really this extends beyond tracking their WP), but I'm not convinced using mechanics to try to give rules to, &quot;don't be a jerk about it,&quot; is ultimately not fixing those problems, and just making the game less fun for people that can make the RAW work, and doing nothing to stop those that would abuse the rules anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:47:46-07:00","id":1301545,"title":"","content":"I dunno it seems easier to me to just be 'don't spend willpower unless it's relevant to the story and the denial leads to something interesting'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T02:35:20-07:00","id":1301558,"title":"","content":"I mean obviously you can still give the characters a willpower stat and treat that as a limit. <br /> <br /> wp 2 peasants can't take more than 2 wp from the pool no matter how many you have left. And if the players try to drain the wp of random people, well, don't resist. Just let them do the influence like you're supposed to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T03:24:27-07:00","id":1301563,"title":"","content":"So, just to be clear here are we only talking about spending willpower to resist social influence? Because that seems to be a lot of what people are saying, which is an entirely different beast than just spending willpower in general, and a different problem I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T03:56:53-07:00","id":1301571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301535#post1301535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the big problem with this is that a ST who is wanting to be able to abuse the system by having NPCs spam willpower for things they really shouldn't by the core rules suggestion is unlikely to agree to being shackled by house rules limiting their ability to do that. I can see why people might be worried about creating the opposite situation where the players try to metagame and willpower tap the ST instead but its a lot easier for a ST to shut that down (or let them but then make them suffer for running around randomly fucking with nobodies for no in character reason except being massive dicks) then it is for a player to do anything about a ST abusing the WP rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's basically where I stand on this, the Storyteller arbitrates every single off-screen interaction there's so many places where they can cheat with this that you're pretty much required to trust them and hope it all works out for the best.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:15:51-07:00","id":1301599,"title":"","content":"The way I run NPC Willpower for an individual character is to ask myself what kind of week they've been having.<br /> <br /> Willpower is spent by people attempting difficult tasks and navigating socially fraught situations. So just like PCs, their Willpower will be full or nearly full if they're well-rested and haven't had to do anything difficult or stressful lately, whereas their pool might be down to a third if they're run off their feet with the situations they're dealing with. A handy default is two-thirds of their pool - they haven't had time to relax lately, but things aren't out of control. Stressed people are easier to pressure/finesse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:34:25-07:00","id":1301605,"title":"","content":"I will say that having some kind of rubric to judge when an NPC should spend wp is probably useful. I\u2019d probably just limit it to one wp per person unless I had a good reason to give them more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T09:12:07-07:00","id":1301649,"title":"","content":"I generally find the best thing is to give NPCs willpower pools that aren't enormous (say, 5; maybe they had more but they spent it), spend it to protect very important intimacies and use charms, but not to use it for minor stuff or extra successes.<br /> <br /> I will say, about NPCs not having to worry about running out... if you're in a fight with Exalts, you're going to want to use all your willpower if it's useful, because otherwise you're going to die.<br /> If you're just a merchant and they're trying to scam you... well, you are going to get a willpower back tonight, so you can maybe spend 1 point.<br /> <br /> And I do track willpower for important NPCs, so for example if a bad guy spends 4wp fighting PCs and then flees (or they flee), and they fight again the next day, he's still going to be 3wp down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:22:06-07:00","id":1301699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301535#post1301535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the big problem with this is that a ST who is wanting to be able to abuse the system by having NPCs spam willpower for things they really shouldn't by the core rules suggestion is unlikely to agree to being shackled by house rules limiting their ability to do that. I can see why people might be worried about creating the opposite situation where the players try to metagame and willpower tap the ST instead but its a lot easier for a ST to shut that down (or let them but then make them suffer for running around randomly fucking with nobodies for no in character reason except being massive dicks) then it is for a player to do anything about a ST abusing the WP rules as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, the issue is less shackling intentionally abusive storytellers than it is helping storytellers balance npc willpower expenditure. Treating it as a resource one has to balance ideally helps make judgments about when it is appropriate to use and when it\u2019d be overdoing it and hobbeling player characters.<br /> <br /> No rule can actually address the problem of a malicious player/storyteller. The only solution is not to play with them. But sometimes restrictions are helpful rails for well intentioned players/storytellers.<br /> <br /> I get the response of \u201cjust use your judgment if the character would resist or not\u201d but that ignores the fact the way that willpower is balanced mechanically isn\u2019t just a question of IF the character would resist, but also having to conserve wp as a resource - and that doesn\u2019t play out with npcs despite the rules treating them the same as PCs in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T11:41:13-07:00","id":1301703,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I really buy the &quot;and that doesn't play out with NPCs,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I've yet to, in multiple editions of Exalted, had well meaning STs/players react in a fashion that's in-line with the problem that seems to be much more theorycraft than application.<br /> <br /> Are STs really having NPCs blow through WP (and motes, and Charms with special reset conditions, etc.) all the time without any consideration for the NPC being a character that would want to conserve things even if mechanically the ST can replenish such resources whenever they want and/or that NPC isn't recurring so it doesn't mechanically matter?<br /> <br /> Following threads here, &quot;STs could,&quot; seems a lot more prominent than, &quot;STs do.&quot;<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> And to make it clear, I'm not against Exalted with some sort of point pool they use to fuel NPCs... but I don't think you can just use it with WP and have it work. We're talking a much more holistic change to how the system treats ST resources and NPCs - which we have plenty of extant games to look to for guidance - to make it actually be the guide rails suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T14:50:50-07:00","id":1301728,"title":"","content":"I think another thing to consider that any pre-created pool is going to be designed to be balanced around a fairly &quot;balanced&quot; session, ie. lots of minor npc's, a few fairly important one and then one or two important ones and they'd be expected to have differing WP based on their importance. <br /> <br /> Exalted gives a lot of power to the players though and if they want to meet a string a powerful NPC's they probably can, which creates a situation where a &quot;pool&quot; could be burned through rapidly even without the intention to be abused, leaving you with the options of breaking your own rules or forced to play a NPC with no WP where they should have lots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T15:15:49-07:00","id":1301732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1301503-storyteller-willpower-pool?p=1301703#post1301703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">II've yet to, in multiple editions of Exalted, had well meaning STs/players react in a fashion that's in-line with the problem that seems to be much more theorycraft than application.<br /> <br /> Are STs really having NPCs blow through WP (and motes, and Charms with special reset conditions, etc.) all the time without any consideration for the NPC being a character that would want to conserve things even if mechanically the ST can replenish such resources whenever they want and/or that NPC isn't recurring so it doesn't mechanically matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>As either a player or ST, it's not a problem I've found. I've never felt like STs are spamming willpower on minor things because they're not worried about running out like a PC might.<br /> But perhaps other players have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T17:45:56-07:00","id":1301766,"title":"","content":"Since I generally am the storyteller I have a set method for npc's that I have used since i started running Werewolf and adapted to all other games.<br /> Important npc main villain use standard creation rules.<br /> NPC average or random use 2 d10 1-05 1 06-20 2 21-45 3 46-55 4 56-65 5 66-75 7 76-85 8 86-95 9 96-100 10 <br /> This gives me a quick, yet fairly even distribution of willpower for any given situation involving small numbers in the event of a large scale say a dynast party with a 100 guests I would probably roll a few times no more than 5 and establish an average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T18:00:45-07:00","id":1301768,"title":"","content":"My NPCs are mostly - but not entirely - quick stats with numbers chosen to be a relative challenge level. If they're chumps, then the Circle can out-roll them without major Essence. If they're on par, then they roll about the same pools of dice. If they're a big bad boss, then they're over and above, with other mechanics to support them.<br /> <br /> If Willpower is going to be important to a social Scene, I treat it as being discoverable similar to an Intimacy, but in broad, non-numeric terms. They might find someone to be iron-willed, negotiable, a bit exhausted, beaten down, or simply spineless. <br /> <br /> I want most of my Scenes to be successful if the players interact with it and come up with a solution that matches the story, so perceiving an NPC to be leaning on his Willpower tends to be a clue what's important to them. In the Scenes that aren't successful, the lack of character success is itself a bit of story, so that overlaps a bit in how it works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:34:37-07:00","id":1302174,"title":"","content":"I never spend WP on behalf of my NPCs (well, almost never). If it's really an issue, just roll WP and take a point for every success. That's what the NPC has to spend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}